CI/CD Pipeline Project Documentation
Project: Deploying a Sample WAR Application from Jenkins to Apache Tomcat on AWS EC2

Objective
Create a Jenkins Freestyle job to deploy a sample WAR application to Apache Tomcat using the Deploy to Container plugin.
Architecture
AWS EC2 (Ubuntu) hosts Jenkins and Apache Tomcat. Jenkins builds/deploys sample.war to Tomcat Manager.
Prerequisites
Ubuntu EC2 (8GB RAM,30GB), Java 21, Jenkins, Apache Tomcat 9, Security Groups (8080 Jenkins,8081 Tomcat).
Implementation Steps
1. Launch Ubuntu EC2 and update packages.
2. Install Java and verify.
3. Install Jenkins and complete initial setup.
4. Install Apache Tomcat, change connector port to 8081, start Tomcat.
5. Install Jenkins 'Deploy to Container' plugin.
6. Create a Freestyle project.
7. Download sample.war into Jenkins workspace.
8. Configure Tomcat users with manager-script role.
9. Configure Tomcat Manager context and restart Tomcat.
10. Add Jenkins credentials (deployer/deployer).
11. Configure Post-build Action -> Deploy war/ear to container.
12. Build the job and verify deployment at http://<EC2-IP>:8081/sample/.
Validation
Successful build in Jenkins console and sample application accessible through Tomcat.
Outcome
Automated deployment from Jenkins to Apache Tomcat using Jenkins Deploy to Container plugin.
Notes
Replace hard-coded IP addresses and passwords with placeholders or secrets before publishing to GitHub.
